.TH OMX-CONTRACT 1 2026-10-17 omx-contract "User Commands"
.SH NAME
omx-contract \- validate, format and render the FreeMixer declarations
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B omx-contract validate
.RI [ input ]
.br
.B omx-contract fmt
.RB [ \-\-check ]
.RI [ input ]
.br
.B omx-contract render \-\-target
.BR c | ts | json | lv2
.B \-\-out
.I dir
.RB [ \-\-check ]
.RI [ input
.RB [ \-\-package
.IR name ]
|
.B \-\-sheet
.IR fixture.json ]
.br
.B omx-contract semver
.I previous-tag
|
.B \-\-from\-dir
.I dir
.B \-\-from\-version
.I x.y.z
.RB [ \-\-version
.IR x.y.z ]
.br
.B omx-contract links
.RB [ \-\-check ]
.RB [ \-\-root
.IR tree ]
.RI [ input ]
.RB [ \-\-package
.IR name ]
.RB [ \-\-at
.IR package = tree ]...
.RB [ \-\-require\-impl ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B omx-contract
reads the FreeMixer declarations, the JSON data every knob, range and default
is written down in once, checks them against their JSON Schema and the rules a
schema cannot express, and renders them as C headers, a TypeScript module or
one resolved JSON file.
.PP
The
.I input
is the data bundled with the command by default, or one of:
.TP
.BI \-\-data " dir"
a data directory;
.TP
.BI \-\-contract\-dir " dir"
a contract directory, where each package installs its own definitions;
.TP
.B \-\-installed
the installed contract directory:
.B $OMX_CONTRACT_PATH
if set, else the
.I contractdir
that
.B pkg\-config
reports for omx-contract.
.PP
A contract directory input takes
.BI \-\-needs " package" @\(aq>= x.y.z\(aq
(repeatable) to require a package at a release, and
.B \-\-json
to print a refusal as JSON on standard output as well.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B validate
Check the input against the schema and the semantic rules.
.TP
.B fmt
Rewrite the input in the one formatting, or with
.B \-\-check
only report the files that differ.
.TP
.B render
Write the C, TypeScript, JSON or LV2 (Turtle) render of the input into
.IR dir ,
or with
.B \-\-check
compare it with what
.I dir
already holds.
.TP
.B semver
Report whether the version bump covers every change since a previous release.
.TP
.B links
Check that each value's source links still name the code they cite.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 is a pass, 1 a failure naming what failed, and 2 a usage or environment
error, which is never a pass. A refusal of the contract directory reader
prints its contract.* code first on the line.
.SH EXAMPLES
Render the union of the installed contract directory as JSON:
.PP
.RS
omx-contract render \-\-target json \-\-out build/contract \-\-installed
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pkg\-config (1)
.PP
https://github.com/FreeMixer/omx-contract
